16/12/if-your-boss-could-do-your-job-youre-more-likely-to-be-happy-at-work\">If Your Boss Could Do Your Job, You're More Likely to Be Happy at Work</a> - “Although we found that many factors can matter for happiness at work – type of occupation, level of education, tenure, and industry are also significant, for instance – they don't even come close to mattering as much as the boss' technical competence.”</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:46:39.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-engineering-team-management","categoryHTML":"<h2>Engineering to Management Transition</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://css-tricks.com/mistakes-ive-made-as-an-engineering-manager/\">Mistakes I've Made as an Engineering Manager</a> - Mistakes: “1) Thinking people give feedback the way they want to receive it; 2) Trying to do everything yourself; 3) Communicating something one time is enough; 4) You have to have everything together all the time.”</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:44:58.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-engineering-team-management","categoryHTML":"<h2>Cognitive Tools</h2><h3>Collections</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.foundingfuel.com/article/gigerenzers-simple-rules/\">Gigerenzer's simple rules</a> - The reason we often relies on these simple heuristics: “outside the lab, in real world, we cannot do well with just with logical rationality, we need ecological rationality - the kind of thinking that helps us get what we want in an environment that's uncertain and dynamic. This means exercising our instincts, using simple but robust rules of thumb.”</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:44:58.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-engineering-team-management","categoryHTML":"<h2>Meetings</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://billwadge.wordpress.com/2019/03/24/laws-of-the-universe-and-teaching/\">Wadge's Law (of Meetings)</a> - “Before every formal meeting there's a smaller, more exclusive, less formal meeting where all the important decisions are made.”</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:44:58.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-engineering-team-management","categoryHTML":"<h2>Re-organizations</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://jessitron.com/2021/05/26/a-high-resilience-org-chart/\">A high-resilience org chart</a> - “If you know what problem you're solving and you know how to solve it, a bureaucratic organization will do. Stick with what you know. If you're writing software, that's a generative activity. You need a high-resilience org chart. Fewer boxes, more flexibility.”</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:44:58.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-engineering-team-management","categoryHTML":"<h2>Recruitment</h2><h3>Interview</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://staysaasy.com/leadership/2021/04/12/the-intangible-skills-you-cant-interview-for.html\">The Intangible Skills You Can't Interview For</a> - “1) Cut-Through on Crappy Tasks; 2) Knowing How to Finish; 3) Knowing How to Start; 4) Giving (And Receiving) Diagonal Feedback; 5) Harnessing the Value of Intangibles.”</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:41:37.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-iam","categoryHTML":"<h2>Authentication</h2><h3>Multi-Factor</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://syslog.ravelin.com/2fa-is-missing-a-key-feature-c781c3861db\">2FA is missing a key feature</a> - “When my 2FA code is entered incorrectly I'd like to know about it”.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:40:24.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-falsehood","categoryHTML":"<h2>Networks</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.netmeister.org/blog/urls.html\">URLs: It's complicated…</a> - There's a lot of components in an URL, and all have their own logic.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-07-03T11:37:16.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-engineering-team-management","categoryHTML":"<h2>Roles</h2><h3>Consultants</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://dabit3.medium.com/the-prosperous-software-consultant-5dc8d705c5dd\">The Prosperous 